      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Using a while‑true loop without a break statement creates an infinite loop that never terminates and can dangerously consume memory.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "A Java for‑each loop iterates over all elements of an array or collection without needing an explicit index or boolean condition.",
        "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0002", "Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "A Java for‑each loop can only iterate forward; it cannot iterate from the end of an array to the beginning.",
        "refs": ["Q0004"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    }
  ],
  "formulas": [],
  "procedures": [
    {
      "procedure_name": {
        "text": "Print each element of a string array using a for‑each loop",
        "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0002", "Q0003"]
      },
      "prerequisites": null,
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Declare and initialise a string array, e.g. `String[] fruits = {\"Apple\", \"mango\", \"orange\"};`",
          "refs": ["Q0001"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Write a for‑each statement: `for (String fruit : fruits) {`",
          "refs": ["Q0002", "Q0003"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Inside the loop body, print the current element, e.g. `System.out.println(fruit);`",
          "refs": ["Q0003"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Close the loop with a closing brace `}`.",
          "refs": ["Q0003"]
        }
      ],
      "outcomes": null,
      "content": {
        "text": "The for‑each loop iterates over the array, assigning each element in turn to the variable `fruit`, and prints each element, producing the same output as an equivalent indexed for loop.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      }
    },
    {
      "procedure_name": {
        "text": "Prevent an infinite while‑true loop by adding a break statement",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "prerequisites": null,
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Start a loop with `while (true) {`.",
          "refs": ["Q0000"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Include a conditional `if` inside the loop that, when satisfied, executes `break;` to exit the loop.",
          "refs": ["Q0000"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Place the remaining loop logic after the conditional, ensuring the break can be reached.",
          "refs": ["Q0000"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Close the loop with a closing brace `}`.",
          "refs": ["Q0000"]
        }
      ],
      "outcomes": null,
      "content": {
        "text": "With a break statement, the while‑true loop will terminate when the break condition is met, avoiding an infinite loop and uncontrolled memory use.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      }
    }
  ],
